WEBVTT

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.730
<i>The Roasting Kneeling!</i>

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.450
<i>An infernal kowtow atop a 
roasting hot iron plate!</i>

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:17.870
<i>Naturally, no one can perform 
this act on their own. Not a one!</i>

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:22.710
<i>Still... you can't escape! 
Not from the Forced Kneeling Machine!</i>

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.210
<i>And yet, there was one 
exception to this rule.</i>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.760
Move it aside. Get that 
machine out of my way!

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:41.470
<i>He endures the Roasting Kneeling!</i>

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:45.120
<i>And from this night that gave birth 
to the most astonishing of legends,</i>

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.440
<i>we rewind the clock...</i>

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.530
<i>The Teiai Group's president, Hyoudou Kazutaka,</i>

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.260
<i>has ordered Tonegawa to devise 
a diabolic game of death.</i>

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.050
<i>Just as he was able to bring together</i>

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:04.410
<i>his team of confusingly-named subordinates...</i>

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:12.670
<i>I think I've lost all the support 
and trust I had with my men.</i>

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>I can't blame them. 
I took the ideas they had suggested,</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.550
<i>slathered them with effusive praise,</i>

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.810
<i>and then turned against them.</i>

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.650
<i>I was dismissive. And then...</i>

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:26.140
<b>Rejected!</b>

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:30.600
<i>I erased them. Wiped it all away.</i>

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.760
<i>It's no different. No different than the 
people I've trampled over in the past...</i>

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.160
<i>The behavior I'd expect of the 
natural-born scum of the world!</i>

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.240
<i>It's disgusting!</i>

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.200
I'm not like them! 
I helped build the Teiai Group!

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.870
I worked my way to get this far, 
over all those years!

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.120
<i>I'll fix this.</i>

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.450
<i>I'm going to make a comeback and 
restore my prestige and honor.</i>

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:59.260
How To Win Your Staff Over:
<b>The Art of Management</b>

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:09.980
<i>Tonegawa Yukio, the number two 
man of the massive Teiai Group.</i>

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.680
<i>He serves the monster of 
the financial sector.</i>

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:17.990
<i>This shot-caller rose to the position 
of President Hyoudou's right-hand man.</i>

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.730
<i>This is the story of the battles 
he waged as a middle manager,</i>

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:26.100
<i>in the shadows of the glory 
and fame he achieved...</i>

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:34.520
<i>The small, unremarkable story... 
about the struggles of a remarkable man.</i>

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:45.140
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:45.140
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:10.270
<i>Agenda 03
<b></b></i>Surefire

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:11.980
So, today,

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.450
to show our gratitude for your 
daily contributions to the company,

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:19.980
we've put together this humble 
overnight company vacation.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:26.390
It's my hope that this trip will serve 
to strengthen the team's solidarity...

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:32.150
And if that leads to further progress 
and eventual success with our project,

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.620
I couldn't ask for anything more.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:35.370
<i>Psst...</i>

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:55.390
<i>The gap between myself and 
the men... They hate me now!</i>

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.590
<i>But I can make the jump!</i>

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:01.280
<i>Tonegawa steps forward, without fear.</i>

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.570
<i>He presses unrelentingly forward!</i>

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:09.430
Well, I can't deny that those 
stuffy reasons are a part of it,

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:13.540
but if you take a look at page three 
of the guidebook you each have...

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.790
Schedule

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.790
Day 1
8:00 Assemble
8:30 Depart
9:30 Arrival
10:00 Lunch
11:00 Entertainment
18:00 Baths
19:00 Dinner
20:00 Entertainment

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.790
Day 2
8:00 Wake up
8:30 Breakfast
10:00 Entertainment
12:00 Lunch
13:00 Entertainment
17:00 Return home

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:18.790
You'll notice entertainment, entertainment,

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.790
The trip isn't over 
until we get back!

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:22.910
entertainment from start to finish! 
That's what this is about: leisure time!

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:28.050
I want you all to forget about work, 
and spend these two days having a good time!

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:32.680
So obvious...

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:34.930
Yamazaki-san?

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:38.930
It's so damn obvious he's trying 
to get on our good side.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:45.320
Probably trying to make up for that horrible 
crap he pulled in the last meeting...

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.590
<b>Trip Guidebook</b>

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.080
But it's having the opposite effect!

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:50.120
It's impossible!

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:53.850
A company trip where the 
employees can actually relax...

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.340
As long as our boss is around,

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:58.830
we're going to be on pins and needles 
trying to avoid pissing him off!

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.390
Tsk! What a pain in the ass!

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:03.080
I can't believe my weekend is blown.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:05.710
Like we're gonna forgive him that easily!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:08.200
This isn't gonna satisfy anybody!

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:16.920
<i>A blue sky... clean air...</i>

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:20.740
<i>A panoramic view filled 
with picturesque nature!</i>

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:25.190
<i>Standing amid it all is a building 
where devils go to play.</i>

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:28.240
<i>Its name: the Multitude House!</i>

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:28.240
<b>Multitude House</b>

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.740
Wow, the weather's perfect around here.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:36.750
Well?

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.640
A mahjong table, a billiards table,

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:43.880
ping pong tables, along with dart 
boards and a room for karaoke.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:47.530
And we've got the entire place to ourselves. 
We can do whatever we want.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:48.970
E-Excuse me...

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.390
Um... is there a bowling 
alley, by any chance?

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:57.400
<i>Psst...</i>

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:58.890
I-I mean...

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.610
<i>After all this,</i>

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:04.950
<i>the fool is still going to yap 
about how he wants to bowl?</i>

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.650
<i>There's a surge of rage.</i>

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:09.170
<i>But...</i>

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.240
<i>I need to stay calm.</i>

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:20.180
Sorry, but there's no bowling alley here.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:23.950
That said, there is one 
within short driving distance.

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.810
N-No, it's okay!

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:28.630
Sorry! Forget I said anything!

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:29.910
I see.

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:34.050
<i>They're like kids in a high school club.</i>

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:38.140
<i>A bunch of bowling club members</i>

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:42.390
<i>who were forced into joining their faculty 
advisor on a "training camp" to a temple.</i>

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:45.230
<i>Well, no matter.</i>

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:49.510
<i>I just need to regain the 
trust I lost with them.</i>

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:52.740
Yamazaki-san...

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:56.840
Tonegawa-sensei said to meet 
up here in the park, but...

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.740
What do you think he wants us to do?

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.330
How should I know?

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:05.500
I can't even guess what 
that tyrant's thinking.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:07.840
I-I guess you're right.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.110
True.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:10.510
He was out of line.

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.330
<i>It erupts!</i>

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:16.760
<i>Their dissatisfaction with their boss!</i>

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:22.740
<i>A sense of suspicion that could never be 
countered by any ordinary company trip!</i>

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.230
Hey, is that everyone?

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:32.740
If you're not here, raise your hand!

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:34.240
<i>Psst...</i>

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:40.620
We're all here, sir.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.020
I see. Then let's begin.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:54.630
At most restaurants, 100 grams of this 
would cost you tens of thousands of yen...

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.570
The finest quality Kobe beef.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:01.640
A supreme barbecue, and it's all-you-can-eat.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.560
Whoa!

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:06.230
Kobe beef!

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.250
<i>Success! Success!</i>

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.650
<i>And more success!</i>

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:13.240
<i>A gourmet-recommended, 
diabolically-marbled slab of meat!</i>

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.330
<i>And the onslaught continues!</i>

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:19.610
How's that?

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:22.520
Hundreds of thousands' worth 
of wine and champagne.

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:25.910
Just a few selections 
from my personal cellar.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:28.750
You can open up any brand you like.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:31.090
You like... you like...

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:35.930
<i>As the sun shines down, their thirst stirs...</i>

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:38.450
<i>for ice-cold, top-shelf liquor!</i>

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.240
<i>Alpha waves rock their brains!</i>

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:43.020
<i>Truly this is an unrivaled 
form of relaxation!</i>

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:56.020
<i>Tonegawa has opened the path!</i>

00:09:56.020 --> 00:10:00.070
<i>A path to regain the trust 
and honor he had lost!</i>

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:01.850
Um, excuse me.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.330
Is there any beer?

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.830
<i>Psst, psst, psst...</i>

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:09.430
I mean, it's not a barbecue without beer.

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:11.640
You idiot! Again with this?!

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.560
Oh, it's fine.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:18.740
They sell beer here, so I 
didn't bother bringing any.

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:19.720
Go buy some.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.890
Use this to get as much as you want.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:24.270
As much as you want... as you want...

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:25.530
So generous!

00:10:26.410 --> 00:10:29.790
Uh, should I have the 
receipt addressed to Teiai?

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:30.650
Huh?

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.730
Don't bother. It's fine.

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.750
But get real beer!

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:37.690
None of that low-malt or sparkling nonsense.

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:40.700
T-Tonegawa-sensei...

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.450
Go on already.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:44.170
Y-Yes, sir!

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:46.200
<i>He takes control</i>

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.760
<i>of this barbecue to bring him 
back from the edge of defeat,</i>

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:51.210
<i>to earn back the trust of the men in black!</i>

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:54.210
<i>But there was still one...</i>

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:59.810
<i>One man who still clung to his 
rage toward Tonegawa: Yamazaki!</i>

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:02.470
<i>To be continued!</i>

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:09.020
I can feel it coursing through my veins!

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:11.800
<i>Amidst the abundant natural beauty,</i>

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:15.400
<i>there is a blasphemous haze of greed!</i>

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:17.400
<i>Meat! Booze!</i>

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.900
<i>Booze! And meat!</i>

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:24.660
<i>Tonegawa's debauched feast is about to begin!</i>

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:27.680
Wow!

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.410
It's so damn cold!

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:32.790
Tonegawa-sensei, where should 
we put the tables?

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:36.550
Oh, over there next to the 
others should be fine.

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:37.490
Yes, sir!

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:38.800
Tonegawa-sensei.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:40.330
What's this newspaper for?

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:42.320
Oh, that's for the fire.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:45.160
Twist up the pages and put them 
between any gaps in the charcoal.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:46.590
Right away, sir!

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:47.560
Sensei!

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:49.220
I got the water you asked for!

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:52.230
Oh, good work. Put it over there, would you?

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:53.690
Yes, sir!

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:58.980
<i>Are you guys really okay with this?!</i>

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:02.030
<i>You're gonna forgive him 
for some beef and booze,</i>

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.880
<i>after what he did?!</i>

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.320
Yamazaki.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:10.080
Sorry, but if you're not busy, 
could you grab the plates for the grill?

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.960
Oh, right away.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:17.840
<i>See? In the end, he's giving orders anyway.</i>

00:12:18.610 --> 00:12:20.960
<i>So much for gratitude...</i>

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.970
Tsk. I guess this is it.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:29.320
<i>Psst...</i>

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:37.730
All right, the fire's looking good.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:39.290
It's almost ready!

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.400
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:44.500
Ah, thank you, Yamazaki! 
Bring those over here and...

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:45.640
The thing is...

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:49.160
Yamazaki-san, hurry, please!

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:50.870
That's just it...

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.530
The plates here are rusted over.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:56.040
Look at this!

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:02.300
All of them?!

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:05.850
These two were in the best 
condition I could find, sir.

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:07.470
The others are even worse!

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:10.470
<i>Psst... Psst, Psst...</i>

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:15.850
I think we might have to cancel the barbecue.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:26.400
<i>Without the plates, 
this meat may as well be a dream.</i>

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:30.060
<i>After inflaming your employees' expectations,</i>

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.770
<i>when the time came to cook,</i>

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:34.230
<i>all you could say was, 
"We couldn't. The plates were rusty."</i>

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:36.980
<i>You'll depress them, disappoint them.</i>

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:38.740
<i>All that excitement, frustrated!</i>

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:42.420
<i>And you'll never regain 
their trust! Their support!</i>

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:06.770
Yamazaki! Saemon-saburou!

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:07.770
Sir?

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:10.950
Keep the fire going! 
I'm gonna find something we can use!

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.810
What does he mean by that?

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:14.950
Who knows?

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:18.620
<i>There's no way he'll find something.</i>

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:22.230
<i>A replacement for a grill... 
nothing that convenient could exist.</i>

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:27.470
Yamazaki-san...

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:31.060
Should we put more charcoal on?

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:33.500
I don't think there's any point anymore.

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:34.900
I thought so...

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:39.730
I guess we don't get to eat that Kobe beef...

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:43.380
<i>If I'm being honest, I am disappointed.</i>

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:46.230
<i>It's a shame I won't get 
to eat this Kobe beef.</i>

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:48.840
<i>But that's the way it must be.</i>

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:51.560
<i>It's what he deserves! Karmic retribution!</i>

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:54.240
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:55.550
Sensei!

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:56.410
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.370
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:09.300
You never know what the 
world has in store for you.

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:15.140
Look hard enough, 
and you'll find what you need.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:16.890
No matter what it might be!

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:24.900
Wh-What the heck is that?!

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:28.660
No idea. No idea what it is, but...

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:32.170
No matter how you look at it, 
it's some kind of giant plate for grilling.

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:33.530
And it's brand new!

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:38.040
I found it over in the warehouse.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.850
Nice one, Tonegawa-sensei!

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:41.740
Amazing!

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:42.920
Nice one!

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:45.750
<i>A giant plate... for grilling?</i>

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.980
<i>Psst...</i>

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:50.050
<i>Wait... Is that...</i>

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:56.820
<i>I'm the only one here who has worked 
directly under President Hyoudou.</i>

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:02.310
<i>So I know about the special 
equipment that he ordered once!</i>

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.500
<i>An iron plate for people to kneel on!</i>

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:10.820
<i>I was transferred before I ever saw 
it, so I'm not positive, but...</i>

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:12.620
<i>This size...</i>

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:14.820
<i>Psst, psst... Psst, psst...</i>

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.550
Sensei! It's nice and hot!

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.290
All right, here we go!

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:34.920
I'm gonna be breaking 
in this brand new plate!

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:35.840
Yes, sir!

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.490
Come on, you guys, load this 
thing up! Don't be shy!

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:42.740
Yes, sir!

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:50.370
<i>But wait... If it's in a place like this...</i>

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:55.860
<i>It might just be an actual 
giant grilling plate.</i>

00:16:55.860 --> 00:17:01.090
Okay, I need two or three of you 
to come to the warehouse with me.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:05.030
I found something interesting.

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:13.400
Wha...

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:15.130
What the heck is that?

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:20.010
Move aside, would you?

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:22.020
R-Right!

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:30.200
<i>Psst...</i>

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:33.030
<i>Isn't that...</i>

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:37.290
Tonegawa-sensei, what's this thing for?

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:41.290
Grab me that cabbage and a knife.

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.290
Right!

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:46.040
H-Here you go.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:46.790
Good.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:53.530
There we go...

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.800
Now, gentlemen, watch this!

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:03.560
<i>Ack!</i>

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.210
How handy!

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:08.060
So easy to use!

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:09.780
I get it!

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:12.620
Sensei...

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:14.900
This cross-shaped part up here...

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.570
What do you suppose it's for?

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.730
<i>Th-That's...</i>

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.680
For hanging tongs.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.580
Wow, that's convenient!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:24.870
<i>No! That thing...</i>

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:27.250
<i>It's the Forced Kneeling Machine!</i>

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:32.470
<i>There's no other explanation for that belt.</i>

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:36.250
<i>This iron plate must be 
what I thought it was!</i>

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:37.720
So good!

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.640
That's Kobe beef for you!

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.440
This is freaking delicious!

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:43.240
Fantastic!

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:45.470
The perfect fire!

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:47.720
And the way it grills so evenly...

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:51.480
Finding this plate feels like destiny!

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.380
Sensei, can we cook some more?

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:57.130
Yeah! Keep it coming.

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:58.140
Right!

00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:01.510
<i>I can't tell them... 
They can't know the truth...</i>

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:02.990
Yamazaki.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.410
<i>Psst, psst...</i>

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:12.250
Look... I'm sorry about the other day.

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:13.750
<i>Psst...</i>

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:16.070
This is my way of apologizing.

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:18.200
Have yourself a nice bite to eat.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:19.000
<i>Psst...</i>

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:21.430
<i>Psst, psst...</i>

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:26.010
Well, go on. Here!

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.520
Don't be shy!

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:47.990
How is it? Good?

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:50.520
It's very good...

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:56.000
<i>And so, in spite of Yamazaki's wishes...</i>

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.280
Cheers!

00:19:58.280 --> 00:19:59.910
<i>It's a huge success!</i>

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:02.920
<i>He regains his honor and dispels his infamy!</i>

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:09.640
<i>Tonegawa's indomitable spirit 
lets him climb up from the abyss,</i>

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:11.640
<i>with a miraculous return!</i>

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:18.090
<i>Team Tonegawa unites, 
going into their third meeting!</i>

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:22.820
<i>And then, to harden the 
bonds that have been forged,</i>

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.310
<i>there's entertainment 
and more entertainment!</i>

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:28.930
<i>It's a blowout of entertainment!</i>

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.710
<i>And the finishing touch... What else?</i>

00:20:34.390 --> 00:20:35.710
<i>Bowling!</i>

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:43.630
<b>Teiai Project
Team Tonegawa</b>

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:49.380
All right, everyone, if you 
could smile for me...

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:50.810
Especially the gentleman in the middle.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:57.650
A-A little more naturally, please.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:00.790
There! J-Just like that.

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:02.330
Here we go.

00:21:02.330 --> 00:21:12.830
<b>Teiai Project
Team Tonegawa</b>

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:10.260
<i>This is the story of a lone man who 
struggles between his employer,</i>

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:14.500
<i>the president, and his own 
employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:19.350
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:56.470
Next Time: "Adult!"

00:22:55.530 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Adult</b>
